==English==
{{slim-wikipedia|servant (disambiguation)|servant}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|servaunt|servand||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|servaunt}}, from {{der|en|fro|servant}}, from the present participle of the verb {{m|fro|servir}}. {{doublet|en|sergeant|servient}}. Morphologically {{suffix|en|serve|ant}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|þeġn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɜːvənt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɝvənt/|[ˈsɝvn̩ʔ]|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-servant.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)vənt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is [[hired]] to perform regular [[household]] or other duties, and receives [[compensation]]. As opposed to a [[slave]].
#: {{ux|en|There are three '''servants''' in the household, the butler and two maids.}}
#* {{RQ:Birmingham Gossamer|chapter=I|passage=As a political system democracy seems to me extraordinarily foolish, but I would not go out of my way to protest against it. My '''servant''' is, so far as I am concerned, welcome to as many votes as he can get. I would very gladly make mine over to him if I could.}}
# One who [[serve]]s another, providing [[help]] in some manner.
#: {{ux|en|She is quite the humble '''servant''', the poor in this city owe much to her but she expects nothing.}}
# {{lb|en|religion}} A person who dedicates themselves to [[God]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A professed [[lover]].
# A person of low condition or spirit.

